WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:06.490
Okay, let's cut to the chase: Rayleigh is
a god damn legendary character, that is oozing

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:13.030
charisma, authority and mystery like Trebol
does snort. A character that is respected

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:18.769
by all and has been the main reason that luffy
is now able to challenge actual yonko and

00:00:18.769 --> 00:00:24.689
is back on track to becoming pirate king,
after the most traumatic moment in his life.

00:00:24.689 --> 00:00:35.590
And so, even though we actually don't know
all to much about his past, I want to use

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:39.760
this chance to not only discuss Rayleigh's
character and his role in the story, but also

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.739
delve a bit deeper into the classic trope
of the mentor, and how, if used correctly,

00:00:44.739 --> 00:00:50.489
it can enhance the fabric of a story significantly.
Oh yeah, and why the hell is he called the

00:00:50.489 --> 00:01:10.120
'dark king'? This is the story of the dark
king, silvers Rayleigh.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:14.990
First of all, can we all acknowledge just
how fantastic Rayleigh's introduction was

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:20.110
in the story? Out of all the great ones we
have gotten, I'm thinking Kaido, katakuri

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:26.619
or imu, this might have actually been my favorite
one. I by that I man the entire sequence.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:32.840
It's simply done fantastically, especially
in the anime. There is no music, just that

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:38.800
slave auctioneer suddenly collapsing. Then
we see this giant sitting there, and holy

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:45.520
dawn this huge ass guy must have done something,
right? But he turns around, calls out the

00:01:45.520 --> 00:02:01.119
old man sitting next to him for using something
called Haki and then this.

00:02:01.119 --> 00:02:02.119
-

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:07.600
This is just the right way to reveal an epic
character like this. This has a real shock

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:12.980
effect. And the way that Rayleigh then enters
the hall later, takes a look at the scene,

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:18.480
deduces what happens, before knocking out
all the guards. how could you not be intrigued

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:34.540
by this mysterious old man, that we now know
was the right hand of the pirate king himself.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:35.540
-

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:39.231
Rayleigh's name has actually two sources of
inspiration. One is Sir Walter Raleigh, an

00:02:39.231 --> 00:02:46.030
English 16th-century explorer and privateer.
And the other is a phenomenon known as&nbsp;"Rayleigh

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:50.540
Scattering". Rayleigh scattering refers to
the scattering of light off of the molecules

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:55.379
of the air, thus changing it wavelength. For
example it's light hitting the molecules in

00:02:55.379 --> 00:03:01.600
our atmosphere that give us a blue sky. So
Rayleigh literally scattering Kizaru's light

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:06.680
attacks, seems to be science pun set up by
Oda. The silver in his name of course is a

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:19.840
running theme within the Roger pirates, with
gold Roger, silvers rayleigh and copper Gaban.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:26.090
Personality wise, as most of the former Roger
pirates we have met, Roger, shanks, oden,

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:32.180
and with the obvious exception of buggy, Rayleigh
is an extremely eccentric, charismatic and

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:36.989
joyful person, that seems to be enjoying life
to its fullest. and since the Roger pirates

00:03:36.989 --> 00:03:42.080
in many ways seem to have been quite similar
to the straw hats in terms of their crew dynamics,

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:47.610
it comes as no big surprise that Rayleigh
gets along with all of them quite perfectly

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:53.659
and even more so, is immediately likable for
us readers. After all, this is a guy that

00:03:53.659 --> 00:04:00.299
has the exact same values and approach to
life as our heroes, but more powerful, mature

00:04:00.299 --> 00:04:01.590
and confident.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:12.159
And a 
detail that I found really interesting in

00:04:12.159 --> 00:04:17.600
this context, is that Rayleigh as a character
shares a lot of characteristics with both

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:24.690
zoro and sanji. Hear men out. Just like zoro,
Rayleigh is the first mate of the Roger pirates,

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:30.770
the right hand of the pirate king and the
first person recruited. Both are powerful

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:36.220
swordsmen, that are only second to their captain
in terms of strength. Just like zoro, Rayleigh

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:41.600
also has a scar above his eye, has a bit of
an alcohol problem and just like zoro manages

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:46.030
to get lost a lot, Rayleigh seems to have
a tendency to get shipwrecked, as happens

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:52.210
on his way to Amazon Lilly and after rogers
death, where he is saved by Hachi. And both

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:55.660
seem to enjoy a good battle.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:05:04.950
On the other hand, just like sanji, the first
thing Rayleigh says is how much he loves women.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:10.450
Before showing us his swordsman skills, he
actually stops kizaru, with a quite Sanji-like

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:15.040
kick. Also, as we see in the action house,
he shares sanjis cunningness and tendency

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:22.050
to go on small infiltration missions. He actually
lets himself get captured to steal money from

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:28.740
the slave action that he had lost gambling.
Sanii AND zoro. No wonder you can't help but

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:38.030
find this man awesome.

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:43.250
Now in terms of his role in the story, Rayleigh
in many ways fits the archetypical trope of

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:49.590
the mentor pretty much perfectly. The mentor,
typically is an experienced adviser and confidante

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:54.720
for the protagonist, that passes on his knowledge
and wisdom, so that people can live better

00:05:54.720 --> 00:06:01.810
lives and society can improve. This character,
not always, but very often comes in the form

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:07.610
of the wise old man or woman, that is better
skilled, faster and more experienced than

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:13.820
their student and now pass these traits on
to the them. They may have grown too old for

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:20.210
the task or have their own job to do. Famous
examples include, Yoda in Star Wars or Tony

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:25.760
stark in Avengers Endgame, or to go more into
anime, Biscuit in hunter x hunter or all might

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:32.000
in boku no hero. Their role is to introduce
a new skill and or set of ideas and values,

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:37.160
often hoping to pass the torch because they
know their role in the world is coming to

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:48.430
an end. And of course, most of the time, expect
them to have the same elderly, but powerful

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:57.670
look associated with the Grandpa God. I think
you agree, that Rayleigh hits this description

00:06:57.670 --> 00:07:02.890
perfectly, though compared to some other mentor
figures, he doesn't have to die to get their

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:16.270
disciple on their feet, we're talking Gandalf,
Dumbledore or Jiraya here. For luffy, this

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:22.990
push is replaced by ace's death, a small twist
on the trope here.

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:29.270
Now, What does this mentor role mean for his
relationship with luffy?

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:36.160
Reighley is pretty much the closest luffy
could get to being mentored by Roger himself.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:41.780
Rayleigh is a relic of the pirate kings era,
someone who is respected by everyone, even

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:52.990
marines like garp or even kizaru, who doesn't
seem to have a lot of respect for anyone.

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:57.810
Based on the stories he heard from shanks,
as well as his personal experience with luffy,

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:02.580
he believes him to be the man that Roger has
been waiting for. The man, he started the

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:12.220
great pirate era for in the first place. Luffy
wears his former captains hat, has a similarly

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:19.470
quirky crew and most importantly he has the
same dream as Roger, though we still don't

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:25.210
know what that dream is. and so its now coincidence
that rayleigh thinks of rogers last words

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:31.600
after luffy leaves.

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:32.600
-

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:37.971
Luffy has literally inherited rogers will,
and thus Roger didn't die. Now obvoiusly after

00:08:37.971 --> 00:08:43.220
the events of sabaody and especially marineford,
rayleigh is fully aware, that luffy won't

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:47.940
be able to continue his journey into the new
world at the level he's currently at. And

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:53.710
so its actually rayleigh that proposes and
sets up the time skip and decides to teach

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:58.870
luffy as much as he can in 2 years, so he
actually has a chance against the monsters

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:03.570
waiting in the new world. and so, not only
does he pass his own knowledge and skills

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:08.830
on to him, but also is the one to mentally
help him recover from his trauma and rekindle

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:19.370
his believe in himself and his ability to
protect his crew.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:25.030
And in the manner of any good mentor, despite
being enormously strong and respected, his

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:29.861
time is over. And the fact that despite someone
as strong as him being around, the world is

00:09:29.861 --> 00:09:35.800
still as messed up as it is, also serves to
show us just how powerful this system is and

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:42.670
how difficult it is to change the world.

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:43.670
-

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:48.130
Okay so that's all nice and well, but let's
talk about the elephant in the room. Why is

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:53.470
this man called the dark king? There have
been a number of speculations about this,

00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:58.010
but there are two things here that I want
to highlight. One is the actual meaning of

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:03.760
the Japanese word, meiou. If you watch too
much anime, like I do, you might know the

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:10.060
word maou, which means demon king or devil.
Meiou on the other hand is the literal Japanese

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:16.860
name for pluto, or if you prefer greek over
latin, hades, the king of the underworld.

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:21.110
Now please feel free to theorize as to what
this might mean in the comments, Id love to

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:26.620
hear your ideas. As for me, the quite obvious
meaning here, is that rayleigh, especially

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:32.770
as a user of conquerors haki, was pretty much
a king himself, one of the strongest people

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:38.180
in the world. The fact that this is obviously
not an epithet he picked himself, suggests

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:45.050
to me, that he was seen as the king in rogers
shadow. Almost as powerful, almost as dangerous,

00:10:45.050 --> 00:10:57.230
but since Roger was the one who shone the
brightest, rayleigh was the dark king.

